# 18-sky-stars: the sky sprite's covered-pixel clear (patch 17, struct_obj.inc's skyObj) only where there can be pixels.
#
# All that is drawn under the sky object before it is the stars (drawSky leaves the sky clear above the hills), and a star
# is one pixel in a row that depends only on its number (patch 12's gba_starY). So the stars note that they were drawn
# (gba_starsOn) and which rows they are in (gba_starRow), and skyObj looks only at those rows: none at all under a sun, a
# giant or a ringed planet (stages 2, 4, 5, 6: no stars), about half of them under the Earth, the twin suns and the moons.
# The framebuffer is the same, word for word (frames.py snaps of stages 1, 5, 7, 8 against the build before).

